Explanation
- In Chrome’s DevTools protocol, a `<link rel="preload">` networkRecord gets its initiator tagged as `type === 'preload'`.  
- By short-circuiting when we see that initiator type, any stylesheet that was simply preloaded (and is later swapped to `rel="stylesheet"`) will no longer show up as a “render-blocking” node in Lighthouse’s dependency graph.  
- As a result, the “Critical Request Chains” audit will omit these preload requests, so they won’t be flagged as blocking the main chain.
